  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Polar coordinates locate points by radius and angle, and turn area into a sweep of the radius about the origin.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The polar curve \\( r=\\sin(k\\theta) \\) traces a rose. Change \\( k \\) and count the petals — odd \\( k \\) gives \\( k \\) petals, even \\( k \\) gives \\( 2k \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Polar rose",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "bcPolarCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "The polar rose curve r equals sine of k theta",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "bcPolarDataBtn",
          "panelId": "bcPolarDataPanel",
          "descId": "bcPolarDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "bcPolarDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points around the rose, one per petal-cycle interval",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "θ (rad)",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "r = sin(kθ)",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "(x, y)",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "bcPolarK",
            "valueDisplayId": "bcPolarKV",
            "label": {
              "en": "Petal factor <b>k =</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Petal factor k",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 1,
            "max": 6,
            "value": 3,
            "step": 1
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "bcPolarPetals",
            "label": {
              "en": "petals",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "—"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Polar area is \\( \\tfrac12\\displaystyle\\int r^{2}\\,d\\theta \\) — one of the headline BC integrals.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Polar calculus",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Convert with \\( x=r\\cos\\theta,\\ y=r\\sin\\theta \\). The area swept is \\( A=\\tfrac12\\displaystyle\\int_\\alpha^\\beta r^{2}\\,d\\theta \\). Slope follows from treating \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) as parametric in \\( \\theta \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Conversion",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( x=r\\cos\\theta,\\ y=r\\sin\\theta \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Polar area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac12\\displaystyle\\int r^{2}\\,d\\theta \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Circle",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( r=a \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Cardioid",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( r=a(1\\pm\\cos\\theta) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example · Polar area",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find the area enclosed by \\( r=2 \\). \\[ \\tfrac12\\int_0^{2\\pi}2^{2}\\,d\\theta=\\tfrac12\\cdot4\\cdot2\\pi=4\\pi. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Polar area",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find the area enclosed by one petal of \\(r=\\sin(2\\theta)\\). <p>One petal: \\(0\\leq\\theta\\leq\\pi/2\\).</p>\\[A=\\tfrac{1}{2}\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sin^2(2\\theta)\\,d\\theta=\\tfrac{1}{2}\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\frac{1-\\cos(4\\theta)}{2}\\,d\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{8}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Convert the polar equation \\(r=4\\cos\\theta\\) to rectangular form and identify the curve.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Multiply both sides by \\(r\\): \\(r^2=4r\\cos\\theta\\Rightarrow x^2+y^2=4x\\Rightarrow(x-2)^2+y^2=4\\). Circle, centre \\((2,0)\\), radius \\(2\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
